  "limits": [
    "provider.detected means the provider returned at least one entity; for the drift case it means both versions returned one.",
    "Only the two direct pins are verified. Their dependencies were resolved at install time and are listed in the setup-gem-list output, not locked.",
    "Recorded on the Ruby and platform named in oracle.environment; the CI platform (Linux, Node 22.x and 24.x for the checks) was not exercised for the oracle.",
    "Releases under pins.not_covered exist but were not exercised; no claim is made for them or for any version other than the pins.",
    "Nothing here ran against a server database, a Rails application or a rake task: the oracle loads a schema file into an in-memory SQLite database and reads model metadata, it runs no model query and no migration, so status.runtime_tested stays false.",
